  "components": [],
  "timeoriginalestimate": null,
  "description": {
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1,
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "1. What happens now"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "When a download from the Parts Velocity report finishes, the message that pops up reads \"Success - Data exported successfully.\" That is a general message that could belong to any screen in the application; it does not name the report or say which of the two files was produced."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "2. What should happen instead"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The written description sets the exact wording, and it names both the report and the file type."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Parts Velocity specification, version 5, requirement S6-R9: \"On a successful download, a success toast reads \\\"Velocity report exported (CSV)\\\" or \\\"Velocity report exported (PDF)\\\".\""
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "3. How to see it"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "orderedList",
     "attrs": {
      "order": 1
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Sign in as a user who can see reports and open "
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Reports",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": " > "
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Parts Velocity",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "In the report's own search box type "
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "BRAKECLEAN",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": ", so the view is small enough to download."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Open the three-dot menu at the top of the report and choose "
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Download (CSV)",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": ". Watch the message that appears."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Do it again and choose "
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Download (PDF)",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": ". Watch the message that appears."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Exact test data this was seen with:",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " part number "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "BRAKECLEAN",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": ", locations "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Staging Heavy Duty - 9919",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " and "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Staging Lethbridge - 4310",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": ", date range "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "This Year",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": ", type "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Both",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "4. What was actually shown"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Both downloads showed the same message:"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "{noquote}"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Success"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Data exported successfully."
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "{noquote}"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The expected messages were "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Velocity report exported (CSV)",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " and "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Velocity report exported (PDF)",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "5. What was ruled out"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bulletList",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "It is not a missing message.",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": " A message does appear, and it appears for both file types - it is the wording that is wrong."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "It is not the failure message.",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": " The failure message is correct: when a download is refused, the message the server sends is passed through and shown to the user word for word, which is what the written description asks for."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "It is not one file type.",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": " The spreadsheet and the PDF both show the same general wording."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "It is not a timing problem.",
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": " The message was captured as it appeared, on four separate downloads."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "6. How often"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Every time. Four downloads out of four."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "7. Where it was seen"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Reports > Parts Velocity, on the QA branch, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " "
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Parts Velocity report specification, version 5, requirement S6-R9, which says: \"On a successful download, a success toast reads \u201cVelocity report exported (CSV)\u201d or \u201cVelocity report exported (PDF)\u201d.\" The wording names the report and the file type, which the general message does not."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
